@* Saved on blur, not on every keystroke: the write happens once per edit (matrix ADDR-04).

   The design's field, class for class. Its hint is described rather than shown: the design draws no
   hint under this field, and one more line of text would change the page's height, so the words
   stay available to a screen reader and out of the layout. The error state is this application's
   own - the design has no error state to copy, because nothing in it can fail. *@
<div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-surface-variant flex flex-col gap-2">
    <label class="text-label-md font-label-md text-on-surface" for="delivery-address">Delivery Location</label>

    <div class="relative">
        <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 pl-3 pt-3 pointer-events-none">
            <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-outline" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"
                 stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M12 21s7-6.2 7-11a7 7 0 1 0-14 0c0 4.8 7 11 7 11 M12 12.5a2.5 2.5 0 1 0 0-5 2.5 2.5 0 0 0 0 5" />
            </svg>
        </div>

        @* Two lines, which is a requirement and not a preference: an address is written on two lines
           and the value's newlines are normalised before storage (matrix ADDR-05, ADDR-06). The
           design draws this field on one line, so it stands 24px taller here than in the design.
           The pin is aligned to the first line rather than to the middle of the box. The onchange
           event is the blur, which is where the address is saved. *@
        <textarea id="delivery-address" rows="2" maxlength="200"
                  class="w-full bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant focus:border-primary focus:ring-1 focus:ring-primary rounded-lg pl-10 pr-4 py-3 text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface outline-none transition-colors"
                  placeholder="e.g., Villa Lotus, Canggu..."
                  aria-describedby="delivery-address-hint"
                  aria-invalid="@((Error is not null).ToString().ToLowerInvariant())"
                  @onchange="OnChangedAsync">@Address</textarea>
    </div>

    <span class="sr-only" id="delivery-address-hint">Where should we assemble your setup?</span>

    @if (Error is not null)
    {
        <span class="alert" role="alert">@Error</span>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Address { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Error { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback<string?> OnSave { get; set; }

    private Task OnChangedAsync(ChangeEventArgs args)
        => OnSave.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string);
}
